hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18245","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abdullah said and I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Aslam Abu Imran from Hubayb ibn Mughfil al-Ghifari that he saw Muhammad al-Qurashi standing dragging his lower garment, so Hubayb looked at him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever treads it in pride treads it into the Fire."
"18246","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah informed us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, he said: Aslam Abu Imran informed me from Hubayb al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever treads upon his lower garment in pride treads into the fire of Hell."
"18247","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Aslam that he heard Hubayb ibn Mughfil, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he saw a man dragging his lower garment behind him and treading upon it in pride, so he said: Glory be to Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever treads it in pride treads it into the Fire."
